  "notes": "{暴|あば}れる is an intransitive verb ({自動詞|じどうし}). There is no direct transitive pair.\n\nASPECT ({ている}):\n{暴|あば}れている indicates an ongoing state of violent or wild behavior.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {暴|あば}れ{回|まわ}る - to run wild, to rampage\n- {暴|あば}れ{出|だ}す - to start acting violently\n- {暴|あば}れん{坊|ぼう} - a wild child, troublemaker\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {暴力|ぼうりょく} - violence\n- {乱暴|らんぼう} - violent, rough (na-adjective)\n- {荒|あ}れる - to become rough/stormy (related but different nuance)",
